64,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, I agree! Option A is too chaotic. I want a stable spot where I can actually talk to everyone, not just grab a random desk.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, Option B sounds like a nightmare. I cannot keep resetting my routine. I need a permanent home to protect my short gaps.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, Option B is a financial trap. Every rotation triggers the 6,200 yen fee. We would bleed the budget dry before the year ends.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, I agree. Option B is a financial disaster. But Option C is the only way to make the window disparity explicit and fair, rather than letting it hide in habit.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, Option B is a physical disaster. My body cannot reset its posture every few weeks. I need a permanent, stable anchor to function.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, I agree! Option C is perfect. It gives us a stable home to build real connections, not just random chats. I want us to be a team!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Yumi, Option C is perfect! A fixed, named desk means I never waste my precious gaps searching. I can finally focus!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, Option C is the only fiscally sound choice. One setup, zero recurring fees. We lock the layout and stop the budget hemorrhage.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, Option C is the only way to make the window disparity explicit. We must name who carries the worse end, rather than letting it hide in habit.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, Option C is the only logical choice. A fixed, named desk allows my body to settle permanently. I will not compromise on stability for your social metrics.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Rin, I am so happy you like it too! A fixed spot means I can actually build real friendships with the people next to me, not just nod at strangers.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I am voting for C. A fixed, named desk is the only way to protect my precious morning gaps and keep my focus sharp!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
